      "v": 3,
      "zh": "耶利哥王打发人去见喇合说：「那来到你这里、进了你家的人要交出来，因为他们来窥探全地。」",
      "en": "So the king of Jericho sent this order to Rahab:[NOTE:1] “Turn over[NOTE:2] the men who came to you[NOTE:3]—the ones who came to your house[NOTE:4]—for they have come to spy on the whole land!”",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “and the king of Jericho sent to Rahab, saying.”",
        "Heb “bring out.”",
        "The idiom “come to” (בוֹא אֶל, boʾ ʾel) probably has sexual connotations here, as it often does elsewhere when a man “comes to” a woman. If so, the phrase could be translated “your clients.” The instructions reflect Rahab’s perspective as to the identity of the men.",
        "The words “the ones who came to your house” (Heb “who came to your house”) may be a euphemistic scribal addition designed to blur the sexual connotation of the preceding words."
      ],
